#: Game/Levels/ImpTactic/L07.lean:16
msgid "# And Another One\n"
"Reverse the implication you proved last level.\n"
"# More about §0\n"
"What this level is showing is that you can think about §1 as a function with 2 parameters instead of a function that returns a function. The §2 tactic implicitly understands this point of view.\\\\\n"
"\\\\\n"
"Once your goal is §3, you can §4. This is like saying “in order to prove R, it suffices to prove §5 and prove §6”. You'll notice that §7 automatically creates the two goals for you in such cases.\\\\\n"
"\\\\\n"
"**Aside:** When you've been using §8 to build conjunctions, this has been the same thing as if you had used §9. You can try that out next level if you're so inclined."
msgstr ""

